// Track lock (Gleissperre, Sh 2/Wn 7) as a signal type.
//
// A track lock is a signal with two states, so it is a signal type like any
// other: stop = laid on (the shoe sits on the rail and would derail a vehicle
// running onto it), proceed = laid off. The interlocking sets it — a route
// over it lays it off, flank protection holds it on — and the `lamps` strings
// are what the model shows.
//
// The look is entirely the mod's: bind "sperre_auf"/"sperre_ab" in a
// `signal_models/*.ron` to the shoe's node, or better bind one of them as a
// `motions` entry, and the shoe swings between its two positions over the
// travel time instead of jumping. Nothing in the engine knows what a track
// lock looks like.
(
    // The presentation system only decides the lamp images; a track lock has
    // no aspect of the H/V or Ks catalogue, and the strings below are its own.
    system: Ks,
    rules: [
        // Laid off — a route runs over it.
        (
            when: (route: Some(true)),
            show: (main: Some(Proceed)),
            lamps: ["sperre_ab"],
        ),
        // Laid on: the resting state, and the one flank protection holds.
        (
            when: (),
            show: (main: Some(Stop)),
            lamps: ["sperre_auf"],
        ),
    ],
)
